ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLE (Peter 2026-08-09): deck MECHANICS = deterministic tools, NOT natural-language-to-the-conductor. The driver is an LLM so 'just say close astro-storage' is tempting, but routine deck ops (drop/ribbon/restore/grow/even/list) must be deterministic verbs: predictable every time, instant+free (no model turn for a break-pane), self-documenting (named verb set = the discoverable surface), and they keep the LLM for JUDGEMENT ('which strands are worth up now') not mechanics ('resize %5 to 40 cols'). The conductor, when it acts, CALLS the same verbs rather than driving tmux ad-hoc. Verbs = shared vocabulary for human AND conductor. Supersedes any 'always use NL with the driver' option. Ladder: (a) driver verbs FIRST → (b) mouse for restore-ribbon → (c) promote the 2-3 most-used to bind -n root chords (no Ctrl-b; cost: steals that key from apps-inside). Don't out-tmux tmux; tmux builtins are prefix-bound (Ctrl-b) and think in panes not @strand/registry so they leave state stale (Ctrl-b x kills pane, leaves PANE_KEEPER_ dangling).
